  "_meta": {
    "description": "Synthetic brand lineups for both seed markets and how each fictional model maps onto real open-data anchors. The seed generator reads this file to pick MSRP / list-price anchors, efficiency, range, and competitor sets from the derived snapshots (us/epa_fueleconomy.csv, us/epa_models_2023plus.csv, de/eea_co2_de.csv, de/kba_fz10.csv, eu/eea_co2_eu.csv, de/ev_range_anchors.json). Brand, model and competitor make/model names are all fictional. The real vehicles each competitor stands in for are kept ONLY in the anchor_make / anchor_model / anchor_source_url fields and the eea_anchor_models keys; they exist solely to look up public open-data rows (EPA, EEA, KBA) and for price provenance, and are never written to generated output.",
    "curated_on": "2026-09-10",
    "price_anchor_rule": "MSRP / UVP anchor = median of the listed competitors' base-trim public prices at curation, rounded to nearest 500; trims priced at +8% / +18% / +30% over base. Competitor prices are NOT in the open datasets; the seed generator carries them in this file with source_url and verify=true.",
    "spec_anchor_rule": "US efficiency/range from EPA class x powertrain medians (us/epa_fueleconomy.csv); DE consumption/CO2/power/mass from EEA make-model rows of the listed competitors (de/eea_co2_de.csv); DE BEV range from de/ev_range_anchors.json.",
    "anchor_key_note": "eea_anchor_models use the dataset spellings (KBA/EEA): 'IONIQ5', 'IONIQ6', 'ID.4' (KBA row is 'ID.4, ID.5'). Matching is case-insensitive substring on the model column."
